<template><section v-if="mode==='Future state'"><h2>Vue migration: remaining work</h2><p>The core workspaces run in Vue. These gaps remain visible so the draft does not imply full parity.</p><ul><li>Guided per-Scout session review, manual occurrence controls and activity-file attachments.</li><li>A structured requirement editor and richer weekly-theme tools.</li><li>Trello JSON exchange and further accessibility/manual workbook acceptance.</li><li>The advanced visual tree canvas remains on hold; the curriculum structure editor replaces its navigation entry. The forecaster was deliberately removed.</li></ul><h2>Ideas for future releases</h2><p>These are discussion ideas, not approved requirements or scheduled work.</p><ul><li v-for="idea in ideas" :key="idea">{{idea}}</li></ul><a href="./docs/standalone-vue.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Migration notes and validation</a></section>
 <section v-else><p>Practical guidance for the current Vue interface.</p><div class="filter-panel"><label>Search help<input v-model="query" type="search" placeholder="Workbook, themes, backups…"></label></div><div class="help-layout"><nav class="help-topics" aria-label="Help topics"><button v-for="topic in matches" :key="topic.id" :aria-pressed="active?.id===topic.id" @click="selected=topic.id">{{topic.title}}</button></nav><article v-if="active" class="help-article"><h2>{{active.title}}</h2><p>{{active.text}}</p></article><p v-else>No help topics match your search.</p></div><details class="panel"><summary>Reference documentation</summary><p>These documents also describe workflows in the legacy comparison app; some advanced tools remain pending in Vue.</p><ul><li><a href="./docs/workflows.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Practical workflow reference</a></li><li><a href="./docs/repeat-counts.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Repeat counts and evidence reference</a></li><li><a href="./docs/standalone-vue.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vue migration notes</a></li></ul></details></section></template>
